# Every text file is LF in every checkout, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout (GitHub's Windows runners set autocrlf=true)
# turned assets/*.toml into CRLF: the Windows release shipped different bytes
# from macOS and Linux — in assets/ and in the include_str! fallbacks compiled
# into the binary — and tests that edit asset text by exact substring failed.
# Binary files (PNGs, models, audio) are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
